# ============================================
# 📄 WHAT : Tells git which files must NEVER be committed.
# 🎯 WHY  : Two reasons — SECRETS (.env) and NOISE (node_modules, dist
#           are rebuildable from package.json / src, so committing them
#           only bloats the repo).
# ============================================

# Dependencies — reinstall anytime with `npm install`
node_modules

# Build output — regenerate anytime with `npm run build`
dist

# 🔒 Environment files — real secrets. Commit ONLY .env.example.
# 💬 INTERVIEW: "What if a secret was committed once?" — rotate it (change
# the real password/secret). Deleting the file later does NOT remove it
# from git history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor/OS junk
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
